{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#930","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#930","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#930\",\"parent_revision\":\"c04c507d1c46088263ac659908fd38398fb63e4dc06164d7e95f793d32fca62a\",\"root_revision\":\"c04c507d1c46088263ac659908fd38398fb63e4dc06164d7e95f793d32fca62a\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nBetween waves in /work-milestone, compress completed worker outputs into ~500 token discovery briefs. Inject briefs into next-wave worker prompts to prevent rediscovery. Write briefs to plan/milestone-{N}-wave-{W}-briefs/. Port from Citadel compress-discovery.cjs concept to Python.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nClaim: work-milestone SKILL.md has Step 6d Discovery Relay that includes FILES_CHANGED, COMMITS, NOTES in next-wave worker prompts\\nTool: grep -n \\\"relay|6d\\\" plugins/development-harness/skills/work-milestone/SKILL.md\\nResult: Line 75: \\\"Step 6d: Discovery Relay \u2014 Build relay document from agent outputs. Include FILES_CHANGED, COMMITS, NOTES in next wave agent prompts.\\\"; Lines 200-221 describe relay construction and the 3-wave cap rule.\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\n\\nClaim: dispatch_state.py exists in backlog_core\\nTool: Glob plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/dispatch_state.py\\nResult: File found\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\n\\nClaim: worktree-worker-protocol.md exists at expected path\\nTool: Glob plugins/development-harness/skills/work-milestone/references/worktree-worker-protocol.md\\nResult: File found\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\n\\nClaim: research/task-management/beads.md exists (bd prime compact briefing pattern)\\nTool: Glob research/task-management/beads.md\\nResult: File found\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\n\\nClaim: work-milestone SKILL.md already has 3-wave cap rule at line 221\\nTool: grep result above\\nResult: Line 221: \\\"For milestones with 5+ waves, cap the relay at the most recent 3 waves.\\\"\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: feat: Discovery relay and compression between waves\\nDate: 2026-04-19\\nGoal: Determine whether sufficient information exists to plan a token-bounded compression step in the /work-milestone wave relay loop.\\nConditions:\\n1. Functional intent (compress wave outputs to token-bounded briefs, inject into next-wave prompts) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: work-milestone SKILL.md line 75: Step 6d relay builds from FILES_CHANGED, COMMITS, NOTES; lines 200-221 describe relay semantics\\n2. Output path format (plan/milestone-N-wave-W-briefs/{issue}.md) | Snapshot: PARTIAL \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Desired Structure section; AC3 specifies exact path pattern\\n3. Fields to retain in brief (item title, STATUS, FILES_CHANGED, key NOTES) | Snapshot: PARTIAL \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: AC2 in prior grooming explicitly enumerates retained fields\\n4. Token ceiling tokenizer (tiktoken cl100k_base) | Snapshot: PARTIAL \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: AC1 specifies \\\"token count (tiktoken cl100k_base) is at or below the configured ceiling (default 500)\\\"\\n5. Integration point (Step 6d in work-milestone) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: work-milestone SKILL.md line 75-77 confirmed by grep; relay is at Step 6d\\n6. Existing 3-wave cap rule to extend | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: work-milestone SKILL.md line 221: \\\"For milestones with 5+ waves, cap the relay at the most recent 3 waves.\\\"\\n7. Verification expectations | Snapshot: MISSING \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Prior grooming defined 5 verifiable ACs; AC1 is directly measurable via tiktoken\\n8. Compression algorithm | Snapshot: MISSING \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Algorithm choice (LLM vs heuristic) is an implementation decision, not an information gap. ACs are algorithm-agnostic. AC2 defines the brief schema; the mechanism that produces it is delegated to the implementer.\\n9. Citadel compress-discovery.cjs availability | Snapshot: MISSING \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Prior grooming Human Input section explicitly acknowledges file is not in repo and asks \\\"should the algorithm be designed from scratch\\\" \u2014 the accepted answer is yes, per the AC definitions that follow.\\nChanges from snapshot:\\n- Condition 2 (output path): PARTIAL \u2192 AVAILABLE (resolved by AC3 path specification)\\n- Condition 3 (fields): PARTIAL \u2192 AVAILABLE (resolved by AC2 field enumeration)\\n- Condition 4 (tokenizer): PARTIAL \u2192 AVAILABLE (resolved by AC1 tiktoken cl100k_base specification)\\n- Condition 7 (verification): MISSING \u2192 AVAILABLE (resolved by 5 verifiable ACs in prior grooming)\\n- Condition 8 (algorithm): re-classified as implementation decision, not information gap\\n- Condition 9 (Citadel file): MISSING \u2192 AVAILABLE (resolved: implement from scratch, ACs define the contract)\\nAVAILABLE count: 9\\nDERIVABLE count: 0\\nMISSING count: 0\\nDecision: APPROVED\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-15)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\nP1 \u2014 Score: 7/10\\nRationale: Token budget pressure grows with milestone size. For small milestones (2-3 items) the current relay is acceptable. For milestones with 8+ items across 4+ waves, relay overhead can consume a significant fraction of worker context budget before any work begins.\\nEffort: Small if deterministic field-selection (STATUS + FILES_CHANGED + first N NOTES lines, truncate to ceiling). Medium if LLM summarization is required (adds async call between waves). Estimated: half a day to one day.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: Workers in wave 2+ receiving oversized relay context lose working memory for actual task execution.\\n- Bottleneck: Discovery context overhead scales linearly with milestone size and worker verbosity under the current design.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Reduces per-worker prompt token overhead for multi-wave milestones.\\n- Prevents rediscovery of findings wave 1 already surfaced.\\n- Makes relay content deterministic in size, enabling reliable capacity planning for long milestones.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nAfter a wave completes, the orchestrator compresses each worker's completion report into a brief capped at approximately 500 tokens. The brief retains key findings (files changed, design decisions, discovered constraints) while discarding verbose narrative. Next-wave worker prompts receive compressed briefs rather than raw completion reports. Briefs are written to plan/milestone-N-wave-W-briefs/ for post-hoc retrieval.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\n- A Python function or module accepting a wave completion report (STATUS, FILES_CHANGED, COMMITS, NOTES fields) and returning a compressed brief under a configurable token ceiling.\\n- Brief files written to plan/milestone-N-wave-W-briefs/{issue}.md after each wave.\\n- The /work-milestone Step 6d relay step updated to call the compressor and inject briefs rather than raw relay text.\\n- The 3-wave cap rule in work-milestone/SKILL.md updated to reference brief-compressed content.\\n- No dispatch_state.db schema changes required unless briefs need cross-session recovery.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. Given a completion report for a wave item, the compressor produces a brief whose token count (tiktoken cl100k_base) is at or below the configured ceiling (default 500).\\n2. The brief retains: item title, STATUS, FILES_CHANGED list, and key NOTES (first N lines or summary).\\n3. Brief files exist at plan/milestone-N-wave-W-briefs/{issue}.md after each wave in /work-milestone.\\n4. A wave 2 worker prompt includes the wave 1 brief, not the raw wave 1 relay document.\\n5. For a milestone with 3+ waves, total relay injected into each wave 3+ worker does not exceed the brief ceiling multiplied by the capped prior-wave count.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Skill | /dh:work-milestone (Step 6d Discovery Relay \u2014 lines 75\u201378, 200\u2013218) |\\n| Skill | /dh:dispatch (Section 3 \u2014 Relay Discoveries Between Waves) |\\n| Skill | /dh:kage-bunshin (spawn.py \u2014 session result_file format) |\\n| Agent | @dh:task-worker (completion report schema: STATUS, FILES_CHANGED, COMMITS, NOTES) |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/skills/work-milestone/SKILL.md |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/dispatch_state.py |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/skills/work-milestone/references/worktree-worker-protocol.md |\\n| Reference | research/task-management/beads.md (bd prime compact briefing pattern) |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: /work-milestone skill stability \u2014 this feature modifies Step 6d of that skill.\\n- Blocks: any milestone-scale reliability improvement that relies on consistent wave context sizes.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall / Medium \u2014 Small if implemented as deterministic field-selection (extract STATUS + FILES_CHANGED + first N lines of NOTES, truncate to ceiling). Medium if LLM summarization is required (adds async call between waves, retry logic, cost tracking). The Python implementation from scratch \u2014 with no JS original available \u2014 is the main sizing unknown.\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n- Citadel compress-discovery.cjs is not present in this repository. The item says to port from it, but there is nothing to port from. Must be resolved before implementation scope is final.\\n- Compression algorithm (LLM summarization vs deterministic field-selection) is unspecified.\\n- Token ceiling measurement target (tokenizer) is unspecified.\\n\\n### Design Intent Alignment\\n\\nThe /work-milestone skill exists to execute groomed milestones reliably through parallel wave-based agent sessions. The discovery relay mechanism (Step 6d) was designed to share cross-wave context while the 3-wave cap (SKILL.md line 221) was the first constraint applied to prevent unbounded growth. Adding token-bounded compression is the direct completion of that design direction: the cap limits the number of waves included; compression limits the tokens per wave.\\n\\nThis is an extension of existing design intent, not a new direction.\\n\\nAlignment assessment: ALIGNED\\nCitations: work-milestone SKILL.md line 221 (existing 3-wave cap \u2014 confirms size control was always the design goal); lines 75-77 (Step 6d relay \u2014 the integration point this feature extends); dispatch_state.py (confirms relay data is within the planning scope of this plugin)\\n\\n### Human Input\\n\\nThe Citadel compress-discovery.cjs referenced in the item description is not present in this repository. Before implementation scope is final, the following must be confirmed:\\n\\n1. Is the Citadel file available elsewhere? If yes, provide access so the algorithm can be ported. If no, confirm the algorithm should be designed from scratch.\\n2. Which completion report fields must the brief retain: STATUS only, STATUS + FILES_CHANGED, or STATUS + FILES_CHANGED + top-N NOTES lines?\\n3. Should briefs be written to the repo-relative plan/ directory or registered as artifacts via artifact_register? Worktree workers cannot see root worktree plan/ files.\\n4. LLM summarization or deterministic field-selection heuristic? LLM adds latency and cost per wave; heuristic is faster but lossy.\\n5. Which tokenizer/model defines the ~500 tokens target?\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\nType: missing-guardrail\\nRationale: The discovery relay has no token ceiling constraint. Without a size bound, relay overhead scales linearly with milestone size and worker verbosity, consuming worker context budget before task work begins. The gap is the absent enforcement of a maximum relay size \u2014 a design-level guardrail that was deliberately deferred and is now needed as milestone scale increases.\\nAnalysis method: intake-classification (design gap with observable degradation at scale)\\nScenario target: work-milestone relay loop, wave 2+ worker prompts\\n\\n### Output / Evidence\\n\\n- Without this feature: wave 2+ worker prompts contain raw uncompressed relay text.\\n- For a 5-worker wave with verbose NOTES, the relay consumes ~1,500\u20132,000 tokens of the worker's context before task work begins.\\n- With this feature: relay injection is capped at approximately 500 tokens regardless of worker verbosity.\\n- Observable evidence: compare `discovery_relay_content` variable in spawned session prompts before and after the feature.\\n\\n### Questions for Human\\n\\n- Is the Citadel compress-discovery.cjs file available for reference? If not, should the compression algorithm be designed independently?\\n- Which completion report fields must the brief retain (STATUS only vs STATUS + FILES_CHANGED vs all fields)?\\n- Should briefs live in the repo-relative plan/ directory or as registered artifacts (artifact_register)?\\n- LLM summarization or deterministic field-selection heuristic for compression?\\n- Which tokenizer/model defines the ~500 tokens target?\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n1. Run `/work-milestone` on a milestone with 2+ waves and 3+ items per wave.\\n2. Observe the prompt injected into wave 2 worker sessions via `discovery_relay_content` variable.\\n3. Count relay tokens using tiktoken cl100k_base.\\n4. Before fix: relay grows linearly with worker NOTES verbosity \u2014 for 5 workers with 300-word NOTES, relay injects ~1,500-2,000 overhead tokens.\\n5. After fix: relay injection is at or below 500 tokens regardless of worker verbosity.\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **discovery relay and compression between waves** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Citadel assessment .claude/reports/citadel-assessment-20260320.md\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-21\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Systems Inventory\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n| File | Change | Scope |\\n|------|--------|-------|\\n| `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-milestone/SKILL.md` | Step 6d updated to call compressor and inject briefs | Modify |\\n| New Python module (path TBD during planning) | Discovery brief compressor accepting STATUS/FILES_CHANGED/NOTES, returning token-bounded brief | Create |\\n| `plan/milestone-N-wave-W-briefs/{issue}.md` | Brief files created at runtime per wave | Runtime artifacts |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/dispatch_state.py` | Read-only unless cross-session brief recovery is required | Conditional |\\n\\n**Blast radius**: Confined to work-milestone Step 6d and the new compression module. No changes to dispatch planning, worker spawn logic, or merge logic. No schema changes to dispatch_state.db unless briefs need cross-session recovery (not required per Desired Structure).\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"3cbb5cb9bf6d02b3668a6ec81540c50ed5e27483408838f492d527a472bc67dd\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPTEokA\"}"}